column33:
Neat idea. OS X's clock can be configured via System Preferences to announce the time on the hour, half-hour, or quarter hour, but not every 5 minutes.  For that, save the program below in $HOME/bin/saytime:<p><pre><code>    #!/usr/bin/perl
    use POSIX;    
    system "say", "It is now " . POSIX::strftime("%I:%M %p", localtime);
</code></pre>
Then add the following line to your crontab:<p><pre><code>    */5 * *  * * $HOME/bin/saytime</code></pre>
